sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    %% iMovies Booking and Concurrency-Safe Seat Reservation Flow
    %% Based on actual controllers/bookingController.js implementation

    actor Patron as Cinema Patron
    participant UI as React UI (SeatSelection.jsx)
    participant Auth as Auth Middleware (auth.js)
    participant Ctrl as Booking Controller (bookingController.js)
    participant ShowtimeModel as Mongoose Showtime Model
    participant BookingModel as Mongoose Booking Model
    participant MongoDB as MongoDB Engine (Replica / Server)

    Note over Patron,MongoDB: Phase 1: Auditorium Seat Map Retrieval
    Patron->>UI: Clicks "Select Seats" for a Showtime
    UI->>Ctrl: GET /api/showtimes/:id
    Ctrl->>ShowtimeModel: findById(id).populate('movie').populate('cinema').lean()
    ShowtimeModel->>MongoDB: Query showtime document with embedded seats[]
    MongoDB-->>ShowtimeModel: Return showtime data
    ShowtimeModel-->>Ctrl: Showtime object
    Ctrl-->>UI: 200 OK: { showtime: { seats: [...], movie, theater, price } }
    UI-->>Patron: Renders curved auditorium screen & seat grid

    Note over Patron,MongoDB: Phase 2: Interactive Seat Selection & Booking Submission
    Patron->>UI: Selects seats (e.g. ['A1', 'A2']) & clicks "Confirm Seats"
    UI->>UI: Verifies selection <= 8 seats & checks auth token
    UI->>Auth: POST /api/bookings with credentials: 'include'<br/>Body: { showtimeId, seats: ['A1', 'A2'] }
    Auth->>Auth: Verifies JWT token from req.cookies.token
    alt JWT Missing or Expired
        Auth-->>UI: 401 Unauthorized { error: 'Unauthenticated' }
        UI-->>Patron: Redirects to /login (saves pending_booking)
    else JWT Valid
        Auth->>Ctrl: Forwards request with req.user = { id, email, role }
    end

    Note over Ctrl,MongoDB: Phase 3: Server Validation & Atomic Concurrency Guard
    Ctrl->>Ctrl: Validate payload: showtimeId exists & Array.isArray(seats) && seats.length > 0
    Ctrl->>ShowtimeModel: findById(showtimeId).populate('movie')
    ShowtimeModel->>MongoDB: Fetch current document
    MongoDB-->>ShowtimeModel: Showtime document
    ShowtimeModel-->>Ctrl: Showtime instance

    Ctrl->>Ctrl: Verify all requested seats exist in showtime layout
    Ctrl->>Ctrl: Pre-check: verify none of requested seats have isBooked === true

    Note over Ctrl,MongoDB: CRITICAL ATOMIC STEP: Single-Document Atomic Update
    Ctrl->>ShowtimeModel: findOneAndUpdate({ _id: showtimeId, seats: { $not: { $elemMatch: { seatNumber: { $in: seats }, isBooked: true } } } }, { $set: { seats.$[elem].isBooked: true, seats.$[elem].bookedBy: userId } }, { arrayFilters: [...] })
    ShowtimeModel->>MongoDB: Atomic write query with arrayFilters

    alt Race Condition: Another Patron Booked A1 or A2 milliseconds earlier
        MongoDB-->>ShowtimeModel: Returns null (document query condition failed)
        ShowtimeModel-->>Ctrl: null
        Ctrl-->>UI: 409 Conflict: { error: 'One or more selected seats were reserved just now...' }
        UI->>Ctrl: Auto re-fetch GET /api/showtimes/:id
        Ctrl-->>UI: Fresh seat map with A1/A2 marked red
        UI-->>Patron: Displays conflict warning & updates grid
    else Atomic Lock Acquired: Seats Successfully Reserved
        MongoDB-->>ShowtimeModel: Returns updated Showtime document
        ShowtimeModel-->>Ctrl: updatedShowtime

        Note over Ctrl,MongoDB: Phase 4: Booking Document Persistence
        Ctrl->>Ctrl: Generate unique bookingReference ('IM-' + 6 chars)
        Ctrl->>BookingModel: findOne({ bookingReference })
        BookingModel->>MongoDB: Check uniqueness
        MongoDB-->>BookingModel: null (unique)
        Ctrl->>BookingModel: new Booking({ bookingReference, user, movie, showtime, seats, totalAmount, status: 'confirmed' }).save()
        BookingModel->>MongoDB: Insert into 'bookings' collection
        MongoDB-->>BookingModel: Saved Booking Document
        BookingModel-->>Ctrl: Confirmed Booking Object
        Ctrl-->>UI: 201 Created: { message: 'Booking confirmed', booking }
        UI-->>Patron: Navigates to /booking/confirmation/:id (Boarding Pass)
    end

    Note over Patron,MongoDB: Phase 5: Cancellation & Seat Release Flow
    Patron->>UI: Clicks "Cancel Reservation" in Dashboard
    UI->>Ctrl: POST /api/bookings/:id/cancel
    Ctrl->>BookingModel: findOne({ _id: req.params.id, user: req.user.id })
    BookingModel->>MongoDB: Find booking
    MongoDB-->>BookingModel: Booking document
    BookingModel-->>Ctrl: booking
    Ctrl->>ShowtimeModel: updateOne({ _id: booking.showtime }, { $set: { seats.$[elem].isBooked: false, seats.$[elem].bookedBy: null } }, { arrayFilters: [...] })
    ShowtimeModel->>MongoDB: Release seats in embedded array
    MongoDB-->>ShowtimeModel: update acknowledge
    Ctrl->>BookingModel: booking.status = 'cancelled' and booking.save()
    BookingModel->>MongoDB: Update booking status to 'cancelled'
    MongoDB-->>BookingModel: Saved
    Ctrl-->>UI: 200 OK: { message: 'Booking cancelled and seats released' }
    UI-->>Patron: Displays success alert & updates pass to 'Cancelled'
